/// A parameter referenced in a case other than its declaration.
///
/// The parameter binding goes through the same environment as a local, so this
/// fails for the same reason CaseLocalVariable does.  It is kept separate
/// because a fix that folds case at declaration sites could easily miss the
/// path that binds arguments to parameters.
///
/// Fails with: Undefined variable 'value'.
///
function Twice (Value : Integer) : Integer;
begin
    Exit value * 2;
end

test 'A parameter resolves through any spelling of its name';
begin
    AssertEqual (6, Twice (3));
end
